This is a Next.js + SQLite membership dashboard for a JCI chapter.
Read PRD_Smart_Member_Management_Platform.md and README.md before any change.
The PRD is the spec; the README records where this build deviates and why.

Architecture — do not change without discussing it first:
- Python (src/, scripts/) owns ALL logic: derived fields, health score,
  alert rules, permissions. It runs at build time and emits five
  pre-filtered JSON payloads, one per demo persona, to web/data/.
- Next.js (web/) only renders those payloads, in SERVER components.
- There is no API route for member data, no runtime database, no ORM,
  no auth library. Do not add one.

Rules:
- The app is READ-ONLY on member data. The only thing written at runtime is
  the activity log.
- Permission filtering happens in Python, in src/permissions.py, before the
  JSON is written. Never filter in a React component, and never ship a field
  to the client that the role may not see. Hidden field groups are DROPPED,
  never hidden with CSS.
- Field-group permissions must follow the data into EVERY table, not just
  members. status_events.reason once leaked a removal reason that the
  governance group was correctly hiding. Check new tables against the matrix.
- web/lib/data.ts imports "server-only". Never remove that, and never import
  it from a client component.
- Derived fields (age, deadlines, requirement status, project role, health
  score, WhatsApp group) are computed in src/derived.py or src/health.py.
  Never store them in the database.
- Colours come from web/lib/theme.ts only. Never write a hex literal in a
  page or component. Chart series use the PRD 13.2 values, not the raw brand
  hexes — they were validated for colour-vision separation.
- Never use colour alone: every health band and alert carries an icon and a
  text label too.
- Every table needs an empty state. Blank panels make a demo look broken.
- Keep functions under 40 lines. No class hierarchies. No premature
  abstraction.
- After changing anything in src/ or scripts/: re-run
  `python scripts/export_json.py && python scripts/verify.py`.
  verify.py must exit 0. It checks the seven alert counts against the PRD.
- Do not add features that are not in the PRD. If the PRD is silent, ask.
